Deploy a test pod configured with your github-runner-sa identity and run an API query 
directly from inside the container:

1. Launch an Interactive Test Pod:Attach Identity to Pod

Deploy a temporary debugging container running under github-runner-sa:

    cat <<EOF | kubectl apply -f -
    apiVersion: v1
    kind: Pod
    metadata:
    name: rbac-test-pod
    namespace: default
    spec:
    serviceAccountName: github-runner-sa
    containers:
    - name: curl-box
        image: curlimages/curl:8.6.0
        command: ["sleep", "3600"]
    EOF

Verification: Run kubectl get pod rbac-test-pod to confirm it reaches the Running state.

2. Inspect the In-Pod Token Mount : Inspect Credentials

Check the files injected by Kubernetes into the container:

kubectl exec rbac-test-pod -- ls -la /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/

Verification: You will see three files: ca.crt, namespace, and token.

3. Execute Authenticated API Calls from Inside the Pod:
Live API Query

Query the Kubernetes control plane directly from inside the pod using curl and the mounted token:

# Test allowed query: List deployments (allowed by our Role)
kubectl exec rbac-test-pod -- sh -c '
  TOKEN=$(cat /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/token)
  curl -s -k -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
    https://kubernetes.default.svc/apis/apps/v1/namespaces/default/deployments | head -n 15
'


# Test forbidden query: Get secrets (denied by RBAC)
kubectl exec rbac-test-pod -- sh -c '
  TOKEN=$(cat /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/token)
  curl -s -k -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
    https://kubernetes.default.svc/api/v1/namespaces/default/secrets
'

Verification: The first command returns valid deployment JSON (HTTP 200). 
The second returns an HTTP 403 Forbidden error with a message indicating the ServiceAccount cannot get secrets!

4. Clean Up the Test Workload:Tidy Up.
Remove the test pod:

kubectl delete pod rbac-test-pod

Verification: Run kubectl get pod rbac-test-pod to confirm it is terminated.

Run these commands in your terminal. 
Do you see the HTTP 200 JSON for deployments and the HTTP 403 Forbidden for secrets?



